  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Offer four single words copied from the stem. Exactly one is the helping verb.",
      "Always include the main verb as a distractor.",
      "Other distractors are the subject, object, place, or describing word. Never a second helping verb.",
      "Every stem has one helper plus one main verb. Never stack helpers such as has been or will be.",
      "Never use be, have, or do as the only verb. Those words must help a clear main verb.",
      "Keep a mix of be helpers, have helpers, do helpers, and modals across the pool.",
      "Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands. Use <NAME>, never a real name.",
      "Tier 1 helpers are is, am, are, can, or will, with obvious noun misses.",
      "Tier 3 always uses a verb-looking main verb such as gone, like, hide, or catch as the closest miss."
    ]
  },
